# Clinical domain

- DPEP fields: Demanda, Procedimentos, Evolução, Plano/Encaminhamentos.
- Clinical working notes/formulation are stored separately from administrative patient data.
- Do not describe a separate clinical area as automatically or legally "inaccessible"; access/governance follows purpose and applicable professional rules.
- Secretary endpoints/DTOs must never serialize clinical fields.
- Session finalization is idempotent and auditable.
- Do not overwrite a finalized clinical record silently; use versioning/amendment semantics.
- Active session UX is distraction-free and optimized for few clicks.
- Recording/transcription/AI processing require technical consent gates before provider calls.
- Refusal of recording/transcription/AI must not be represented as resistance and must not impair access to care.
- Never infer that a suggested intervention was performed; procedures require clinician-confirmed evidence.
- Child/adolescent and couple/family/group contexts require source-of-information and modality awareness.
